			<abstract>
<div xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><p>In recent years, deep learning has revolutionized many fields <ref type="bibr" target="#b4">(LeCun, Bengio, &amp; Hinton, 2015)</ref>. One of the most influential architectures is the residual network, which enables the training of very deep convolutional networks <ref type="bibr" target="#b2">(He, Zhang, Ren, &amp; Sun, 2016)</ref>.</p><p>In the field of natural language processing, the introduction of the Transformer architecture marked a paradigm shift <ref type="bibr" target="#b0">(Vaswani et al., 2017)</ref>. Subsequent models such as BERT (Devlin et al.,  2019)  demonstrated that pre-trained language representations could be fine-tuned for many downstream tasks. More recently, large language models have shown remarkable few-shot learning capabilities <ref type="bibr" target="#b3">(Brown et al., 2020)</ref>.</p></div>
			</abstract>
